1
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,270
May the Warrior grant him courage

2
00:01:58,510 --> 00:02:01,270
and protect him in these perilous times.

3
00:02:01,590 --> 00:02:03,750
May the Smith grant him strength

4
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,780
that he might bear this heavy burden

5
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:10,260
And may the Crone, she that knows the fate of all men,

6
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:13,220
show him the path he must walk

7
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:16,280
and guide him through the dark places that lie ahead.

8
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,810
In the light of the Seven, I now proclaim Tommen

9
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:23,000
of the House Baratheon First of His Name

10
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,590
King of the Andals and the First Men

11
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:28,350
and Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

12
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,420
Long may he reign!

13
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,750
Long may he reign!

14
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,890
Special day.

15
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:07,350
Your Grace.

16
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,150
Your Grace.

17
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:38,910
-Your Grace.  -Your Grace.

18
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:54,620
Your Grace.

19
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,600
There he is.

20
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,550
Long may he reign.

21
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:04,290
Long may he reign.

22
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:10,900
He sits the throne like he was born to it.

23
00:04:11,010 --> 00:04:14,260
Yes. He wasn't, though, was he?

24
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,010
No, he wasn't.

25
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:24,620
You still mourn for Joffrey?

26
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,240
He was my husband. My king.

27
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,910
He would have been your nightmare.

28
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,550
Your Grace, I feel.

29
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,630
You knew exactly what he was.

30
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:39,830
I did, too.

31
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:41,930
You never love anything in the world

32
00:04:41,930 --> 00:04:44,080
the way you love your first child.

33
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,060
Doesn't matter what they do.

34
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:53,720
And what he did, it shocked me.

35
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:58,440
Do you think I'm easily shocked?

36
00:04:58,440 --> 00:04:59,540
No.

37
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:03,180
The things he did shocked me.

38
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,580
He's only a boy.

39
00:05:12,170 --> 00:05:14,130
A good boy. A decent boy.

40
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:15,570
He always has been.

41
00:05:16,210 --> 00:05:19,100
Who was the last decent king, I wonder?

42
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:21,120
He could be the first man who sits on that throne

43
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:24,100
in 50 years to actually deserve it.

44
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:28,180
It would be some consolation, wouldn't it?

45
00:05:28,610 --> 00:05:31,230
For all the horror that put him there.

46
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:38,180
He will need help,

47
00:05:39,830 --> 00:05:41,960
if he's going to rule well.

48
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,380
He has you.

49
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,790
A mother is not enough.

50
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:51,260
You're still interested in being queen, I take it?

51
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,910
After all that's happened,

52
00:05:58,010 --> 00:06:00,990
it sounds strange, I know, but I am,

53
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,560
I haven't even given any thought to it,

54
00:06:03,710 --> 00:06:05,420
what comes next.

55
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,920
It would be a great honor, of course.

56
00:06:08,730 --> 00:06:11,510
But I will have to speak to my father about it.

57
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:15,830
Yes, speak to your father.

58
00:06:17,190 --> 00:06:18,670
I'll speak to mine.

59
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:27,220
We may be faced with an alarming number of weddings soon.

60
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,970
I won't even know what to call you.

61
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:33,340
Sister?

62
00:06:35,530 --> 00:06:36,870
Or Mother?

63
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:43,960
King Joffrey Baratheon is dead.

64
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:47,530
Murdered at his own wedding.

65
00:06:47,790 --> 00:06:50,410
And we have taken the Meereenese navy, Your Grace.

66
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:52,760
The Second Sons took the Meereenese navy.

67
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:55,190
Who told you to take the navy?

68
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:56,850
No one.

69
00:06:57,610 --> 00:06:59,840
So why did you do it?

70
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:01,400
I heard you liked ships.

71
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:07,280
How many ships?

72
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,660
93, Your Grace.

73
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:10,120
How many men can they carry?

74
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,930
9,300, not counting sailors.

75
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:15,070
Would that be enough to take King's Landing?

76
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,250
The Lannisters have more.

77
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:19,350
They've been fighting Joffrey's wars for years.

78
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:21,290
They're tired, dispersed.

79
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:22,770
And now their king is dead.

80
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:27,190
8,000 Unsullied, 2,000 Second Sons,

81
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:29,070
sailing into Blackwater Bay

82
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:31,870
and storming the gates without warning.

83
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:38,210
It's hard to say. It could be enough.

84
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:41,420
But we're not fighting to make you queen of King's Landing.

85
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,330
10,000 men can't conquer Westeros.

86
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:46,370
The old houses will flock to our queen

87
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:48,000
when she crosses the Narrow Sea.

88
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,670
The old houses will flock to whichever side they think will win,

89
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:52,270
as they always have.

90
00:07:55,070 --> 00:07:56,550
There's other news.

91
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,730
From Yunkai.

92
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:02,300
Without the Unsullied to enforce your rule,

93
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:05,320
the Wise Masters have retaken control of the city.

94
00:08:05,470 --> 00:08:07,960
They've reenslaved the freedmen who stayed behind

95
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:10,270
and sworn to take revenge against you.

96
00:08:11,810 --> 00:08:13,720
And in Astapor,

97
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:16,590
the council you installed to rule over the city

98
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:19,790
has been overthrown by a butcher named Cleon

99
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:22,820
who's declared himself "His Imperial Majesty."

100
00:08:25,250 --> 00:08:26,840
Please leave me.

101
00:08:32,310 --> 00:08:33,950
Not you, Jorah.

102
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:51,300
It appears my liberation of Slaver's Bay isn't going quite as planned.

103
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:55,370
You could sail for Westeros

104
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:57,270
and leave it all behind.

105
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:59,030
A boy sits on the Iron Throne.

106
00:08:59,030 --> 00:09:02,420
A boy many believe to be a bastard with no right to it.

107
00:09:03,530 --> 00:09:05,440
They've never been more vulnerable.

108
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:08,850
You counseled me against rashness once in Qarth.

109
00:09:09,430 --> 00:09:10,770
I didn't listen.

110
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:14,350
That all worked out well.

111
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:23,030
How can I rule seven kingdoms

112
00:09:23,350 --> 00:09:25,820
if I can't control Slaver's Bay?

113
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,540
Why should anyone trust me?

114
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:32,560
Why should anyone follow me?

115
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,070
You're a Targaryen.

116
00:09:34,070 --> 00:09:35,900
You're the Mother of Dragons.

117
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,990
I need to be more than that.

118
00:09:47,290 --> 00:09:51,430
I will not let those I have freed slide back into chains.

119
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,640
I will not sail for Westeros.

120
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:56,430
What, then?

121
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,860
I will do what queens do.

122
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:05,430
I will rule.

123
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,060
Pull up your hood.

124
00:10:45,630 --> 00:10:47,470
A memorable shade.

125
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,200
But how would they know?

126
00:10:50,570 --> 00:10:53,720
You know what kind of stories poor men enjoy the most?

127
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,650
Ones about rich girls they'll never meet.

128
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:03,760
Is this the only way into the Eyrie?

129
00:11:04,070 --> 00:11:05,610
The mountains are impassable.

130
00:11:06,050 --> 00:11:07,470
If you want to get to the Eyrie,

131
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:09,440
you need to go through the Bloody Gate.

132
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,040
It doesn't matter how large your army is,

133
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:15,790
if you attack this gate, you do it on this road,

134
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:17,370
three men abreast

135
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:20,210
and get slaughtered like goats.

136
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:23,360
The first Lords of the Vale didn't have much,

137
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,960
but they had these mountains

138
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,920
and they knew how to use them.

139
00:11:27,380 --> 00:11:29,670
And the fortress they built here has never been overcome.

140
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:31,820
Not once in 1,000 years.

141
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,350
Know your strengths, use them wisely,

142
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:38,550
and one man can be worth 10,000.

143
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:45,680
Who would pass the Bloody Gate?

144
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:49,030
Lord Petyr Baelish and his niece Alayne.

145
00:11:53,490 --> 00:11:54,650
Stand to.

146
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:56,770
-Stand to!  -Stand to!

147
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:00,500
Welcome back, Lord Baelish.

148
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,670
Uncle Petyr!

149
00:12:35,070 --> 00:12:36,400
My Lord.

150
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:49,110
I have brought you a gift.

151
00:12:53,760 --> 00:12:55,170
Lord Baelish.

152
00:12:55,170 --> 00:12:57,600
-My Lady.  -Look what Uncle Petyr brought me.

153
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:00,410
A beautiful gift for a beautiful boy.

154
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:03,730
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance, Lady Arryn.

155
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:05,010
My name is Al.

156
00:13:05,010 --> 00:13:07,490
Oh, do take down that hood, child.

157
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,930
Don't you think I know who you are?

158
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:14,330
You think I'd let my intended leave the Eyrie on urgent business

159
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,690
without knowing what that business was?

160
00:13:18,250 --> 00:13:22,220
I let him go, so he could bring you here to me.

161
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:28,140
My flesh and blood.

162
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:32,750
It's wonderful to meet you, Aunt Lysa.

163
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:34,710
You mustn't call me that in front of anyone else.

164
00:13:34,710 --> 00:13:35,940
Of course. I understand.

165
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,380
No one can know you're here.

166
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:39,790
It would put us in a very precarious position.

167
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,320
I would never say a thing.

168
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,430
The Lannisters want to destroy us.

169
00:13:43,430 --> 00:13:45,350
They've been trying for years.

170
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,710
Now they know what it feels like.

171
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:49,660
Mummy said they killed your mother

172
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,810
and they chopped off your brother's head.

173
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:56,780
They did, and my father's.

174
00:13:57,050 --> 00:13:59,530
They killed my father, too, with poison.

175
00:14:00,570 --> 00:14:03,420
I wanted to make the little Lannister baby man fly,

176
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,790
but Mother said I couldn't.

177
00:14:05,790 --> 00:14:07,110
Make him fly?

178
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:09,620
Through the Moon Door.

179
00:14:14,690 --> 00:14:16,350
And on top of everything else,

180
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:18,910
they made you marry that filthy troll.

181
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,260
They did. They made us both.

182
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,640
Lord Tyrion didn't want to.

183
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,790
I don't believe that for a moment.

184
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:26,890
Did he force himself on you?

185
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:28,380
No.

186
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:30,210
-We never.  -Good.

187
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:33,230
Robin, this is your cousin Sansa.

188
00:14:33,230 --> 00:14:35,320
But you're not to call her Sansa in front of anyone,

189
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,650
but Uncle Petyr and myself. Do you understand?

190
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,120
Sansa, this is my son Robin.

191
00:14:41,410 --> 00:14:43,100
It's a pleasure to meet you, Robin.

192
00:14:43,370 --> 00:14:45,360
Robin, show Sansa to her chamber.

193
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,850
Take the back stairs.

194
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,880
Go. We'll speak soon.

195
00:15:02,090 --> 00:15:03,640
What took you so long?

196
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:06,670
Arranging for the ascension of King Tommen I,

197
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:10,070
extricating Sansa, getting her here alive.

198
00:15:10,070 --> 00:15:11,070
She's here.

199
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:14,100
We've spent more than enough time on her for one evening.

200
00:15:16,610 --> 00:15:18,480
Let's get married tonight.

201
00:15:18,490 --> 00:15:19,730
Ought we not

202
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:23,680
inform the Lords of the Vale about the ceremony?

203
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,790
There's only one Lord of the Vale.

204
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,410
The others can all hang.

205
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:30,010
Lurking and simpering on the stairs like buzzards

206
00:15:30,010 --> 00:15:31,790
the moment my husband died,

207
00:15:31,790 --> 00:15:33,350
trying to get their claws in me.

208
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:34,690
I do think that we could wait until.

209
00:15:34,690 --> 00:15:37,010
I'm done waiting, Petyr.

210
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:39,730
We had our wedding night many years ago.

211
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:42,200
Or don't you remember?

212
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:43,890
Like it was yesterday.

213
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:48,260
What wife would do for you the things I've done for you?

214
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:52,170
What wife would trust you the way I've trusted you?

215
00:15:52,730 --> 00:15:54,640
When you gave me those drops

216
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,300
and told me to pour them into Jon's wine,

217
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:58,910
my husband's wine,

218
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:02,180
when you told me to write a letter to Cat

219
00:16:02,190 --> 00:16:04,370
telling her it was the Lannisters.

220
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:18,530
The deed is done.

221
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,810
Faded into nothing.

222
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,240
Only speaking of it can make it real.

223
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,620
Tonight it is, then.

224
00:16:33,690 --> 00:16:35,840
Let me bathe and dress for the occasion.

225
00:16:35,860 --> 00:16:39,190
Once I'm presentable, I'll call on the septon immediately.

226
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,810
I'm warning you.

227
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:52,580
I'm going to scream when my husband makes love to me.

228
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:55,740
I'm going to scream so loud,

229
00:16:55,740 --> 00:16:58,490
they'll hear me clear across the Narrow Sea.

230
00:17:23,730 --> 00:17:26,950
When will the wedding take place in your mind?

231
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:28,850
As soon as decency permits.

232
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,290
After we've allowed Tommen

233
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:32,870
the appropriate time to mourn his brother

234
00:17:33,630 --> 00:17:35,470
and Margaery to mourn her husband.

235
00:17:35,470 --> 00:17:37,870
-A fortnight?  -That seems reasonable.

236
00:17:38,650 --> 00:17:41,290
No jugglers, no jousting dwarves,

237
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:44,330
no 77-course meals.

238
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,620
And your wedding to Loras?

239
00:17:50,010 --> 00:17:51,390
Shortly after Tommen's.

240
00:17:51,390 --> 00:17:53,540
-Shortly?  -A fortnight.

241
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,920
I know you don't like them.

242
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,050
I didn't like your husband.

243
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:02,010
Used to pat me on the back a lot.

244
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,610
I didn't trust him.

245
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,400
We had that in common.

246
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:09,170
You don't need to make formal alliances with people you trust.

247
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,840
Then whom can we trust?

248
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:15,020
Ourselves alone.

249
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:19,760
The Tyrells

250
00:18:20,470 --> 00:18:22,640
are our only true rivals

251
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,640
in terms of resources

252
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:27,670
and we need them on our side.

253
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,160
Robert wasn't particularly rich.

254
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:32,790
Robert had me funding him.

255
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:36,750
Wars swallow gold like a pit in the earth.

256
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:40,100
I suppose that explains why we did so well in the last one.

257
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:41,670
Do you know how much gold

258
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:44,240
was mined in the Westerlands this past year?

259
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,340
Haven't a clue.

260
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:47,140
Go on, your best guess.

261
00:18:48,030 --> 00:18:49,980
Pounds, tons, ounces?

262
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:51,980
Doesn't matter. The answer is the same.

263
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,720
That can't be.

264
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:58,240
Our last working mine ran dry three years ago.

265
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:01,000
Then how do we pay for anything?

266
00:19:01,190 --> 00:19:03,590
The crown owes the Iron Bank of Braavos

267
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,570
a tremendous amount of money.

268
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:06,490
How much?

269
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,340
A tremendous amount.

270
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:14,430
There must be someone at the Iron Bank

271
00:19:14,430 --> 00:19:16,710
you can speak to, come to some arrangement.

272
00:19:16,710 --> 00:19:18,530
The Iron Bank is the Iron Bank.

273
