Who?

541
00:35:06,710 --> 00:35:08,110
A Kingsguard.

542
00:35:12,060 --> 00:35:15,120
He tried to kill Lord Tyrion at the Blackwater.

543
00:35:18,990 --> 00:35:20,880
How did you kill a Kingsguard?

544
00:35:23,380 --> 00:35:25,960
I pushed a spear through the back of his head.

545
00:35:37,620 --> 00:35:39,190
Bloody ridiculous.

546
00:35:43,630 --> 00:35:45,440
Help me with these straps.

547
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:08,070
Hey, get up.

548
00:36:09,100 --> 00:36:10,260
Get up.

549
00:36:17,850 --> 00:36:19,740
That's it, lad, put it inside.

550
00:36:20,030 --> 00:36:22,000
Get the fire going again. We're all freezing.

551
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,560
Aye. What we need is a girl there.

552
00:36:24,570 --> 00:36:25,900
I've got to have a piss.

553
00:36:39,190 --> 00:36:40,610
Now keep quiet.

554
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:23,740
You need water.

555
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:26,230
It doesn't matter.

556
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:28,490
Of course it matters.

557
00:37:32,150 --> 00:37:34,110
You mustn't let anything stop you.

558
00:37:36,470 --> 00:37:38,180
They already have stopped me.

559
00:37:39,470 --> 00:37:40,630
No.

560
00:37:43,980 --> 00:37:45,290
You're not here.

561
00:37:51,910 --> 00:37:53,410
You're far from here.

562
00:37:56,340 --> 00:37:57,750
What does that mean?

563
00:38:04,260 --> 00:38:05,460
At the hill.

564
00:38:07,210 --> 00:38:08,910
A great weirwood tree.

565
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:13,040
You've seen it, too.

566
00:38:13,730 --> 00:38:16,830
Meera and I, even Hodor,

567
00:38:18,580 --> 00:38:20,430
we're only here to guide you.

568
00:38:24,530 --> 00:38:26,040
He's waiting for you.

569
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:30,230
We have to find it.

570
00:38:31,950 --> 00:38:33,700
You have to make it.

571
00:38:34,950 --> 00:38:36,220
We will.

572
00:38:37,500 --> 00:38:40,580
This isn't the end.

573
00:38:42,450 --> 00:38:43,810
Not for you.

574
00:38:45,200 --> 00:38:46,580
Not yet.

575
00:38:47,290 --> 00:38:48,530
How

576
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:51,540
will we know the end?

577
00:39:04,010 --> 00:39:05,310
You'll know.

578
00:39:18,660 --> 00:39:19,880
Brothers.

579
00:39:21,900 --> 00:39:23,510
You do move quiet.

580
00:39:25,960 --> 00:39:28,090
-How many?  -11 men.

581
00:39:28,450 --> 00:39:30,180
Most of them already drunk.

582
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:33,630
No guards posted. They don't seem to have a care in the world.

583
00:39:33,730 --> 00:39:35,910
We'll carve them up like walnut pie.

584
00:39:36,750 --> 00:39:39,430
Karl was a top paid cutthroat in Flea Bottom.

585
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,600
I've seen what he can do with a knife.

586
00:39:41,610 --> 00:39:43,630
Have you seen what I can do with a knife?

587
00:39:44,880 --> 00:39:45,940
Not yet.

588
00:39:48,470 --> 00:39:50,180
There's a hut on the west side of the keep.

589
00:39:50,180 --> 00:39:52,090
We should steer clear of it.

590
00:39:52,120 --> 00:39:53,170
Why?

591
00:39:53,170 --> 00:39:55,650
They've got some hounds chained up inside.

592
00:39:56,500 --> 00:39:59,410
Closer we can get without the dogs sniffing us, the better.

593
00:40:00,830 --> 00:40:02,320
New moon tonight.

594
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:07,610
Get some rest.

595
00:40:08,460 --> 00:40:10,080
We move at sundown.

596
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:14,190
I've always liked a girl with curls.

597
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:16,030
A touch of class.

598
00:40:16,650 --> 00:40:18,290
You take whatever's left.

599
00:40:22,380 --> 00:40:23,670
Get her up.

600
00:40:25,660 --> 00:40:26,770
Stop.

601
00:40:27,180 --> 00:40:28,330
Stop. What are you doing?

602
00:40:28,330 --> 00:40:31,140
Hodor. Hodor. Hodor.

603
00:40:31,140 --> 00:40:31,910
Stop.

604
00:40:32,810 --> 00:40:33,880
Stop!

605
00:40:34,920 --> 00:40:36,460
-Hodor. Hodor.  -Stop!

606
00:40:38,460 --> 00:40:40,660
-Please.  -Hodor.

607
00:40:40,660 --> 00:40:43,770
-Please, get off her!  -Hodor. Hodor.

608
00:40:43,770 --> 00:40:46,410
Please! Please, leave her alone!

609
00:40:49,450 --> 00:40:51,340
Please, stop. Stop.

610
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:54,140
-What are you doing? Leave her alone!  -Hodor. Hodor.

611
00:40:54,680 --> 00:40:55,340
No!

612
00:41:06,230 --> 00:41:08,350
You've got pretty hair, don't you?

613
00:41:10,100 --> 00:41:12,990
Now what is a pretty little highborn girl like you

614
00:41:12,990 --> 00:41:15,810
doing out here in the deep, dark woods, eh?

615
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:21,400
You left your daddy's castle looking for trouble, didn't you?

616
00:41:21,710 --> 00:41:23,480
No dresses for you.

617
00:41:25,200 --> 00:41:27,160
You like it rough, don't you?

618
00:41:28,120 --> 00:41:30,590
You like it in the gutter, don't you?

619
00:41:31,410 --> 00:41:33,800
If you let my sister go, I can help you.

620
00:41:35,490 --> 00:41:37,130
You can help me?

621
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:38,860
I can.

622
00:41:41,160 --> 00:41:42,820
And how you gonna do that?

623
00:41:46,700 --> 00:41:50,300
I have the sight. I can see things.

624
00:41:50,660 --> 00:41:52,330
That's very helpful.

625
00:41:52,330 --> 00:41:54,410
Things that haven't happened yet.

626
00:41:58,410 --> 00:41:59,970
What a fine thing.

627
00:42:03,610 --> 00:42:04,730
A fine thing.

628
00:42:07,120 --> 00:42:09,520
Have you seen what I'm gonna do to your sister?

629
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:16,040
Have you seen what they're going to do to your sister?

630
00:42:18,580 --> 00:42:19,240
No.

631
00:42:22,760 --> 00:42:24,510
Don't close your eyes.

632
00:42:30,900 --> 00:42:32,460
I saw you die tonight.

633
00:42:35,370 --> 00:42:37,220
I saw your body burn.

634
00:42:38,250 --> 00:42:41,570
I saw the snow fall and bury your bones.

635
00:42:45,380 --> 00:42:46,650
To arms!

636
00:42:47,810 --> 00:42:49,330
They're here, the Night's Watch.

637
00:43:19,950 --> 00:43:21,500
Rescue party is here, lads.

638
00:43:22,950 --> 00:43:23,680
Lady.

639
00:43:23,770 --> 00:43:25,410
-Is Jon with you?  -Aye.

640
00:43:27,110 --> 00:43:28,170
I'll take you to him.

641
00:43:31,650 --> 00:43:33,070
You're Brandon Stark?

642
00:43:38,850 --> 00:43:40,100
Hodor. Hodor.

643
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:43,430
The little crippled lord. We're going for a ride, boy.

644
00:43:43,430 --> 00:43:44,970
Jon! Jon!

645
00:43:45,510 --> 00:43:48,960
Keep talking and I'll cut your friends' throats.

646
00:43:49,730 --> 00:43:52,230
Starting with the idiot. Do you hear?

647
00:43:53,490 --> 00:43:54,580
Do you hear?

648
00:44:07,530 --> 00:44:08,620
Hodor! Hodor!

649
00:44:11,200 --> 00:44:12,420
Hodor. Hodor.

650
00:44:13,130 --> 00:44:15,150
Hodor. Hodor.

651
00:44:18,010 --> 00:44:19,880
Hodor. Hodor. Hodor.

652
00:45:03,340 --> 00:45:04,220
Hodor.

653
00:45:06,430 --> 00:45:09,620
Hodor, get his knife. Cut me loose.

654
00:45:11,130 --> 00:45:13,830
Hodor, get his knife.

655
00:45:15,760 --> 00:45:17,060
Cut me loose, Hodor.

656
00:45:23,770 --> 00:45:26,410
Jojen and Meera, free them.

657
00:45:27,130 --> 00:45:27,840
Go!

658
00:45:43,440 --> 00:45:44,230
Jon!

659
00:45:46,700 --> 00:45:48,460
If he sees you, he won't let you go north.

660
00:45:48,700 --> 00:45:51,210
-He's my brother.  -And wants to protect you.

661
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:53,280
He'll take you back to Castle Black.

662
00:45:55,790 --> 00:45:56,760
You have to decide.

663
00:45:57,750 --> 00:45:59,350
Do you want to find the three-eyed raven?

664
00:46:14,390 --> 00:46:16,930
-Hodor.  -Hodor.

665
00:46:17,010 --> 00:46:18,280
We need to free Summer.

666
00:46:19,500 --> 00:46:20,540
And we need to go.

667
00:46:36,170 --> 00:46:37,190
Lord Snow.

668
00:46:38,580 --> 00:46:40,030
Are you bringing me back for trial?

669
00:46:43,250 --> 00:46:44,350
We had a good thing here.

670
00:46:45,510 --> 00:46:46,790
We were free men.

671
00:46:47,840 --> 00:46:49,060
You'll never be free.

672
00:46:50,350 --> 00:46:52,050
You'll never know what that's like.

673
00:47:13,900 --> 00:47:15,310
You learn how to fight in a castle?

674
00:47:21,580 --> 00:47:23,650
Some old man teach you how to stand,

675
00:47:24,050 --> 00:47:25,110
how to parry?

676
00:47:29,360 --> 00:47:30,650
How to fight with honor?

677
00:47:44,760 --> 00:47:45,930
You know what's wrong with honor?

678
00:47:57,480 --> 00:47:58,470
You.

679
00:48:30,690 --> 00:48:31,690
Are you all right?

680
00:48:35,340 --> 00:48:36,190
Come with me.

681
00:48:38,080 --> 00:48:38,850
Come on.

682
00:48:56,660 --> 00:48:57,770
We lost four brothers?

683
00:48:59,470 --> 00:49:00,260
Five.

684
00:49:04,160 --> 00:49:05,970
What the seven hells could do that to a man?

685
00:49:08,990 --> 00:49:10,710
I count 10 dead mutineers.

686
00:49:12,140 --> 00:49:13,520
Locke said there were 11 of them.

687
00:49:15,530 --> 00:49:16,570
Where's Rast?

688
00:50:01,330 --> 00:50:02,460
-Here's another.  -Jon.

689
00:50:06,880 --> 00:50:08,070
Where in seven hells?

690
00:50:10,110 --> 00:50:10,920
Come here.

691
00:50:18,560 --> 00:50:19,840
I missed you, boy.

692
00:50:24,680 --> 00:50:25,920
What should we do with this lot?

693
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:33,380
It's not safe for you here on your own.

694
00:50:34,260 --> 00:50:36,120
Mance Rayder has an army heading this way

695
00:50:36,120 --> 00:50:37,780
and there's worse out there than Mance.

696
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:42,980
Come with us to Castle Black.

697
00:50:44,320 --> 00:50:46,620
We can find you work. Keep you safe.

698
00:50:46,920 --> 00:50:49,080
Meaning all respect, Ser Crow,

699
00:50:49,560 --> 00:50:52,430
Craster beat us and worse.

700
00:50:53,580 --> 00:50:55,770
Your brother crows beat us and worse.

701
00:50:56,220 --> 00:50:57,630
We'll find our own way.

702
00:50:58,210 --> 00:50:59,310
You want to stay here

703
00:51:00,690 --> 00:51:01,730
in Craster's Keep?

704
00:51:06,250 --> 00:51:07,520
Burn it to the ground

705
00:51:08,720 --> 00:51:10,510
and all the dead with it.

